From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 06:38:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 19/27] feat: shape mask as an optical element - pupil = mask
 INTERSECT iris, continuous
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The mask and the iris stay two separate mechanisms (mask value field vs blade polygon, each with its own edge ring) but the pupil is their physical intersection at every f-number instead of a hard swap at Mask Aperture: with k = N_mask / N the polygon trims the silhouette's corners for k > 1 and clips it progressively for k < 1, the gather kernel importance-samples the same clipped pupil (rebuilt in quantized iris steps from the kept mask pixels), and the splat energy gain divides by the pupil's measured fill instead of a constant. Depth of field and blur follow the pupil's bounding circle (max(N, N_mask)); light reaching the sensor is area(iris ∩ mask)/area(iris) integrated from the mask on the component side, times the new Mask Open Area (tint of the open parts), through the T-stop term so exposure and grain react like an ND loss. User-verified.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017nykaDjTHxHDSo11CsYx6M
